<!--
    futura-audio/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml

    Central string resource catalog for the Futura Audio app module.

    This file contains every user-visible string across all six feature
    phases. It is the single source of truth for:
      • App identity (launcher name + camouflage alias name)
      • Widget labels (referenced from res/layout/widget_now_playing.xml)
      • Wake-Up Overlay copy (Phase 1)
      • Now Playing copy (Phase 2)
      • Library, DJ, Visualizer, Car Mode, Sleep Dock, Privacy Vault (Phases 3–6)
      • Notifications, permission rationales, and error messages
      • Accessibility content descriptions

    ── Conventions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    • Keys are prefixed by surface: `wake_*`, `nowplaying_*`, `library_*`,
      `dj_*`, `visualizer_*`, `car_mode_*`, `sleep_*`, `privacy_*`,
      `alarm_*`, `perm_*`, `error_*`, `widget_*`. This lets translators
      batch by context and lets developers grep by surface.
    • `_cd` suffix marks a contentDescription (accessibility) string.
    • `_format` suffix marks a string with positional args (%1$s / %1$d).
    • `_placeholder` suffix marks fallback text the runtime overwrites.
    • Localization: no string is hard-coded in Kotlin / Compose / XML
      layouts. If a future screen needs a new label, add it here first.

    ── Forward references ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Some strings describe UI that does not yet exist (e.g., Car Mode
    speed-dial labels, Visualizer framerate buttons). They are declared
    now so that when the corresponding Compose screens are written they
    can reference @string/… directly without a follow-up edit to this
    file. None of these strings creates a compile-time dependency — they
    are inert until referenced.
-->
